=== the rule's thesis, quoted ===
  A guarantee about a type holds only over the operations through which the type can be observed. Every
  public field, every accessor returning something the invariant does not cover, and every constructor
  that does not re-establish the invariant is a hole in the guarantee, not a stylistic matter.

